      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Crystal Caverns, Fragment of Fear [zone=870]\n**Who:**\n- Captain Dunstan Coldheart [npc=41295]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Dreadstone Compass [item=106359]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Engineer Colle [npc=41630]\n- a Ry`Gorr miner [npc=41612]\n- a Ry`Gorr scout [npc=41616]\n- a Ry`Gorr watchman [npc=41618]\n- a crystal glare lord [npc=42102]\n- a spinechiller spider [npc=41619]\n- a tentacle terror [npc=41621]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Crystal Caverns #1: An Abundance of Orcs [quest=6044]\n- Crystal Caverns #2: Ry`Gorr Reconnaissance [quest=6045]\n- Danela's Stand [quest=6048]\n- Into the Caverns of Fear [quest=6047]\n- Raid Expedition: Danela's Stand [quest=6049]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 20:45:55 2012\nModified: Thu Feb 6 06:02:54 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the third task in a series of three. It is a solo task that begins with Captain Dunstan Coldheart ( map \\- full zone map) in the Crystal Caverns (located in a room in the center of the Coldain city, Froststone at -255, 230, -400)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"An Abundance of Orcs\"\n\\- Completed \"Ry`Gorr Reconnaissance\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Dunstan Coldheart'\nCaptain Dunstan Coldheart says 'This shard that Danela is hoarding appears to be releasing fear into the atmosphere, transforming the creatures that dwell here into something more monstrous. The effect it appears to have on sentient beings is alarming as well. We must [find] the fear shard before we all fall victim to its corruption. Or have you come to me for [other reasons]?'\nYou say, 'Let's find it'\nCaptain Dunstan Coldheart says 'Danela could have hidden the shard anywhere. The caverns are vast, and we simply don't have enough time to canvas every nook and crevice searching for something we've never even seen. The one thing we know is that this crystal shard is emitting powerful fear that is able to penetrate the minds and bodies of all it comes into contact with. This sort of disturbance doesn't go unnoticed, but we need to find a way to better [detect] it.'\nYou say, 'How do we detect it?'\nCaptain Dunstan Coldheart says 'Froststone is home to an [engineer] who has created many innovative gadgets over the years. He is a bit awkward and withdrawn, but I believe his imagination and craftsmanship are what will help us find this fear shard.'\nYou say, 'Who is the engineer?'\nCaptain Dunstan Coldheart says 'His name is Colle. He keeps himself secluded on the upper floor of Froststone. Speak with him and explain the situation. Hopefully he'll be able to craft something to help us locate the shard.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Finding the Fear '.\nCaptain Dunstan has asked you to aid Engineer Colle in creating an item that can locate the fear shard.\nThe reclusive inventor named Colle should be able to create an item capable of locating the fear shard. He's known to linger on the second floor of Froststone.\n\n---\n\nSpeak to Engineer Colle 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Engineer Colle ( map \\- full zone map) is found on the second level of Froststone._\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Colle'\nEngineer Colle focuses on the floor as you recount the details surrounding the hidden fear shard. The reclusive coldain inventor thinks for few moments before an enlightened smile spreads across his face. 'Oh, this is a clever idea, indeed!' Clearly pleased with himself, Engineer Cole decides to share some details with you. 'Since the hidden shard seems to radiate fear, I will craft a compass whose needle will point you to large clusters of fear. I still have some details to work out, but I have a list of items that I'll require.'\n\n---\n\nCollect Flawless Terrorite from tentacle terrors 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\nCollect Velium Sheet Metal from Ry`Gorr orcs 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\nCollect a Spinechiller Fang from a spinechiller spider 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Task Window Says:_ Colle has asked you to collect various items he'll need to craft his compass.\n_The above updates occur randomly from kills (no item looting involved)._\n\n---\n\nReturn to Engineer Colle 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that you have everything Colle has requested, return to the engineer and see if he can craft the compass.\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Colle'\nEngineer Colle takes the requested items for you and begins to assemble the gadget with dexterous coordination. In a matter of moments, the dwarf has the compass complete and places it in your hands. 'It's a rather ingenious device, if I do say so myself. It's powered by small amounts of fear essence found within creatures, and when charged, the needle will point to large concentrations of fear. Good luck!'\n_You receive a \"Dreadstone Compass\"._\n\n---\n\nKill fear-tainted creatures to power the Dreadstone Compass 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Task Window Says:_ In order to power the compass, you'll need to kill tentacle terrors and spinechillers.\n_Kill tentacle terrors and spinechiller spiders to progress this step. This will take 5-7 kills. You will see emotes as you kill the mobs:_\nThe compass needle moves slightly as the essence of fear is harnessed.\nThe Dreadstone Compass is fully charged and ready for use.\n\n---\n\nUse the Dreadstone Compass to locate where the fear shard is being kept 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Task Window Says:_ The compass should point in the direction of concentrated fear.\n_Right-click the compass to generate a path which will lead you to a random area. Once you get to the area, a named spawns._\nDefeat a crystal glare lord 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Task Window Says:_ An evil eye has appeared through a crack in the cavern wall. Kill it before it kills you!\nA crack opens up in the wall, revealing a new area within the caverns.\n_The glare lord fight is on par with standard trash mobs._\n\n---\n\nReport back to Captain Dunstan Coldheart 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n_Task Window Says:_ Dunstan is expecting a full report.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Dunstan Coldheart'\nCaptain Dunstan Coldheart appears relieved to see you. 'My guards reported a cave in fairly close to Froststone, exposing a hidden portion of the caverns. I hadn't heard from you and began to wonder if you had fallen victim to the icy rubble. At least we know where the shard is located. I've sent a team of scouts ahead to investigate the newly exposed area within the caverns. Thank you for risking your life for Froststone. I speak on the behalf of all coldain when I express our gratitude.'\nYou found the location of the fear shard within Crystal Caverns, but were unable to retrieve it.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience (3 AAs + 2-3% exp in Level 96)",
