      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Crystal Caverns [ToV]\n**Who:**\n- Andera Velmist [npc=55069]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Crystal Glue [item=138041]\n- Crystal Spider Capture Harness [item=138040]\n- Crystal Terror Capture Harness [item=137989]\n- Moving Ice [item=138043]\n- Rock Dust Coated Moving Ice [item=138052]\n- Sympathetic Ice [item=138053]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Roderick Coldheart [ _Quests_]\n- a geonid fragment [npc=55592]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Crystal Caverns (10 Points) [quest=9798]\n- Spider Eggs [quest=9768]\n- Spider Harness [quest=9769]\n- Supply Run [quest=9767]\n**Era:** | !Torment of Velious\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Oct 28 01:44:15 2019\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Torment of Velious Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**You can get this task from Andera Velmist in the dwarf fort in Crystal Caverns at +165, +473, -380 on the 2nd floor in the dwarf fort. Findable via Ctrl+F.**\nYou say, 'Hail, Andera Velmist'\nAndera Velmist says, 'Oh, thank Brell. Were you [ **sent**] to us?'\nYou say, ' No one sent me.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'Hrm. Well. I guess that's not important. If you got here through all of the creatures surrounding Froststone, you must be an able adventurer. That means you can help us solve our [ **problem**].'\nYou say, ' Another dinky place with a dinky problem calling on adventures to help, but hey, I don't have anything better to do.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'I'm not sure I like your attitude, but we do need help. Not too long ago, there was a massive noise, unlike anything we have heard. It resonated through the crystal of these caverns. And after that, the ice began to move. It isn't fast, but that doesn't matter because, well, it's ice! Ice shouldn't [ **move**]!'\nYou say, ' Norrath is an amazing place, but yes, ice that moves is weird.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'Yeah. Creepy. We're afraid that it will grow and take over if we don't do something about this. If your [ **willing**] to assist, we'll start by helping Roderick. Keep your eyes open; I'll want to know if you see anything odd about the creatures you kill for him.'\nYou say, ' Yeah Yeah. I'm willing.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Invading Ice'.\nAndera Velmist says, 'Good. Thank you.'\n\n---\n\n_Andera Velmist is concerned about the moving ice. Help her see if Froststone can do something to get rid of the ice._\n_Assist Roderic Coldheart to examine the effects of the ice on the creatures besieging Froststone._\n1\\. Assist Roderick Coldheart with the task Crystal Geonids 0/1 (ALL)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n2\\. Assist Roderick Coldheart with the task Crystal Terrors 0/1 (ALL)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n3\\. Assist Roderick Coldheart with the task Crystal Spiders 0/1 (ALL)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n4\\. Report anything [ **interesting**] you found while assisting Roderick 0/1 Crystal Caverns\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'Yes, there were some interesting things.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'Good. Good. So tell me about the [ **geonid**].\nYou say, 'The geonid are acting a bit weird. While they fight back, they don't seem to have the same spark or care that I've seen from geonid before.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'That is odd and something to consider. Maybe the ice is doing something to them. What about the [ **terrors**]?\nYou say, 'The terrors are violent and territorial, but that seems normal.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'At least something is normal. And, as I'm sure you've guessed, I'd like you to tell me about the [ **spiders**].\nYou say, 'Now there is an issue. The spiders are no longer alive. That ice has infused their bodies and is animating them. The creepy factor is tenfold because they still act like spiders, but slightly off. It's distrubing.\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nAndera Velmist says, 'Thank you. I'll consider what this means. I'll likely ask you to do more research, but something's come to my attention. Well, I knew it, but Cassia reminded me. We are in dire need of supplies. Go help Cassia.'\n5\\. Assist Cassia Gemshard 0/1 (ALL)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nComplete the Supply Run [quest=9767] quest for Cassia.\n6\\. Speak with Andera Velmist 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nAndera Velmist says, 'Thank you. We'll be able to keep going for a while longer. I've had a thought about what to do next. Get some spider eggs. Their young will be a good barometer of the problem.'\n7\\. Spider Eggs 0/1 (ALL)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou have been assigned the task ' Spider Eggs [quest=9768]'.\n_Search for Spider Eggs_\n8\\. Deliver Spider Eggs 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nAndera Velmist says, 'I don't see [ **any spider eggs**]. Did you find any?'\nYou say, 'I did not find any spider eggs. Do you like sending adventurers on wild goose chases?'\nYour task, 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nAndera Velmist says, 'Well. It wasn't my intention to send you on a pointless errand. And, the fact that there are no eggs is information. The more knowledge we accumulate, the better off we'll be. Since they keep duplicating, but they are not laying eggs, the spiders themselves may tell us what we need to know. So, go [ **capture a spider**] alive, undead, or whatever. Bring it to the empty room on the upper level to the south.'\n9\\. Bring a live spider to the empty room, on the upper level to the south 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'How do I capture a spider?'\nAndera Velmist says, 'How should I know? You're the adventuring type. But, maybe someone here in Froststone can help you. You'll probably need something to stun it and a harness to keep it from attacking you while you drag it here.'\nHead over to Hursa Brightsteel [npc=55085] (under the banker) and request her task Spider Harness [quest=9769]\nOnce you've obtained the harness, head back to Roderick and tell him ' **I need to help Andera**'. Crystal Glue [item=138041] will appear on your cursor.\nGo find a spider and DPS it to under 20%, then right-click the Crystal Glue [item=138041] on it, then right-click the Crystal Spider Capture Harness [item=138040] on it, then bring it to the empty room above Grabble Coldheart. [npc=55077]\nDo not use invisibility or invis vs. undead at this point or you will lose the spider and will have to redo the step.\n_The glue binds the spiders joints. It looks less agile._\n_You captured a spider!_\nUpon bringing the spider to the empty room:\n_You tie the lead to a box._\nYour task 'Invading 'Ice' has been updated\n10\\. Speak with Andera Velmist 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'Hail, Andera Velmist'\nAndera Velmist says, 'Good. I'll get to studying the spider you provided. It will also be useful to see why the terrors are not affected. So please [ **capture a terror**]. Please the terror in the west room on the upper floor.'\nYou say, 'Fine. I'll capture a terror. It would have been nice to do both at once!\n_Again, head to Hursa Brightsteel and metion you must 'Capture a terror'. She will give you 'Crystal Terror Capture Harness_\nYou say, 'Capture a terror.'\nHursa Brightsteel says, 'A terror now? Well. I'd try this harness. You'll probably want to weaken them before you try and place it. Good luck.'\n_Now go DPS a terror to below 20% and bring it to the west room on the upper floor._\n_You tie the lead to a box._\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\n11\\. Bring a live terror to the empty room, on the upper level to the west 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n12\\. Speak with Andera Velmist 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'Hail, Andera Velmist'.\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nAndera Velmist says, 'So you said that the geonids are acting strange. Particularly passive. See if you can ask them about the ice and get a coherent answer.'\n13\\. Speak with a geonid about [ **moving ice**] 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'Moving ice.'\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nA geonid says, 'Ice is cold. Cold not bad. But ice not ice. Squirming. Tickles. Good. Bad. Not sure. Taste. But like water. Water near out. Water make cooler.\n14\\. Collect a sample of Moving Ice 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n_Head down to cave past the lake with the broken bridge, to the triple split of spiders, terrors, and geonids. Stand just at the geonid entrance to receive task update and a piece of Moving Ice is placed on your cursor._\n_/way 174, 535, -548 is where this step updates at. Not far from the Eastern Wastes zone in just out from the geonids through the cave. The location will vary around that area so it will be different for each character of the group._\n_You use your weapon to break off a piece of moving ice._\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\n15\\. Deliver 1 Moving Ice to a geonid\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nTurn-in the Moving Ice to any geonid.\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\n16\\. Kill 2 geonid fragment 0/2 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n2x _A geonid fragment (lvl 99)_ spawn. Kill for update.\n_You have been given: Rock Dust Coated Moving Ice_\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated\n17\\. Report your findings to Andera Velmist 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'Hail Andera Velmist.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'So. What did you [ **find out**] from the geonid?\nYou say, 'I found out that you should not feed geonid the moving ice.'\nAndera Velmist says, 'So what happened? Did it [ **attack you**]?'\nYou say, 'Not really. It didn't attack me. Instead, it vomited the ice back up; its arms fell off. Then the arms turned into tiny geonid that attacked! In the meantime, its arms grew back.'\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nAndera Velmist says, 'That is odd behavior, but it's all adding up. Give Hursa Brighsteel the moving ice and see what she can make from it.'\n18\\. Deliever 1 Rock Dust Coated Moving Ice to Hursa Brightsteel 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\n_You have been given: Sympathetic Ice_\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\nHursa Brighsteel says, 'Yes. This is interesting. I've been listening to your conversations with Andera, and, now that I see this ice, I think the geonid imparted something to it. With my study on the spider and the terror, I can envision something that might help. It won't get rid of the moving ice, but it may stop the ice from advancing any further. It will give us time to find a more permanent solution. With that in mind, take this and use it on the ice at the end of the stone near Evercold.'\n19\\. Use Resonating Ice at the end of the stone near Guard Evercold 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nHead over by Guard Evercold (the entrance that leads to the lake). Just where the city ends and the icy part begins, click the Resonating Ice. /loc 345, 625\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\n_The ice shudders. While it's still moving, you think it's no longer growing._\n20\\. Report the results to Andera Velmist 0/1 (Crystal Caverns)\n> **Task Window Text:** ?\nYou say, 'Hail, Andera Velmist'\nAndera Velmist says, 'So. Did Hursa Brightsteel come up with a [ **solution**]?\nYou say, 'Yes. Her solution is a stopgap measure, but it seems to work.'\nYour task 'Invading Ice' has been updated.\n_Andera Velmist is grateful that you h ave given them a solution to combat the moving ice._\n_Andera Velmist says, 'Oh, Thank Brell. And thank you.'_\n_\n---\n_\n_Reward(s):_\n_425 platinum_\n_You gain experience!_\n**Submitted by:** Gidono\n- Platinum",
